    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q1-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"There are 16 ordered marks: Split them into two halves of eight: (a) The fourth and fifth marks are 58 and 60, so Q1 = (58 + 60)/2 . [A1] = 59 (b) The eighth and ninth marks are 60 + a and 60 + b. The middle pair has sum 2(68) = 136, so 120 + a + b = 136. The median of 68 gives a + b = 16. [B1] The distinct digits are in ascending order, so a = 7, b = 9 . [A1] (c) The upper quartile averages the twelfth and thirteenth marks, 70 + c and 70 + d. [B1] The stem has 6 ≤c &lt; d ≤8. [A1] The three averages are (76 + 77)/2, (76 + 78)/2, (77 + 78)/2.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The possibilities (6, 7), (6, 8), (7, 8) give Q3 = 76.5, 77, or 77.5 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 7 marks.</p>"
