    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-g/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The recruitment director of a large accounting firm believes that maths graduates are more successful when applying for positions in his firm compared with graduates of other subjects. One in five job applicants to this firm is successful. The recruitment director selects a random sample of 25 maths graduate applicants. a) Find the critical region to test at the 5% level of significance the director’s belief. State your hypotheses clearly. ( ) 5 b) State the probability of incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis in a test, using the critical region obtained in part (a). ( ) 1\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Ten successful maths graduate applicants were found in the sample. ( ) 2 c) Complete the test.\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Let p be the probability that a maths graduate applicant is successful: Let X count successes in the sample: (a) Test H0 : p = 0.2 [B1] against H1 : p &gt; 0.2. [A1] Under H0, X ∼B(25, 0.2). [A1] Use P(X ≥8) = 1 −P(X ≤7) and P(X ≥9) = 1 −P(X ≤8). The upper-tail probabilities at 8 and 9 are approximately 0.1091 and 0.04677, so the critical region is X ≥9 . [M1] [A1] (b) The actual significance level is the probability of entering the chosen critical region when p = 0.2. The probability of rejection under H0 is P(X ≥9) ≈0.04677 . [A1] (c) The observed 10 lies in the critical region:\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Reject H0. [A1] There is evidence at 5% that maths graduates have a success probability above 0.2 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The recruitment director of a large accounting firm believes that maths graduates are more successful when applying for positions in his firm compared with graduates of other subjects. One in five job applicants to this firm is successful. The recruitment director selects a random sample of 25 maths graduate applicants. a) Find the critical region to test at the 5% level of significance the director’s belief. State your hypotheses clearly. ( ) 5 b) State the probability of incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis in a test, using the critical region obtained in part (a). ( ) 1 Ten successful maths graduate applicants were found in the sample. ( ) 2 c) Complete the test."
