    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-g/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"An airline service operates between Manchester and Madrid. The flight times of this service, in minutes, may be modelled by a Normal distribution with mean of 85 and a standard deviation of 8 . a) Determine the probability that the next flight time of this service will take less than 75 minutes. ( ) 4 ( ) b) Find the time not exceeded by 22.66% of the flights. 4 c) If a flight from this service took less than 95 minutes, what is the probability that the actual flight time was in fact less than 75 minutes. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:592.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:586.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Drawing a diagram:\" style=\"--madas-width:538.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The flight time is X ∼N(85, 82). (a) Standardise to obtain (75 −85)/8 = −1.25. By symmetry Φ(−1.25) = 1 −Φ(1.25). Thus P(X &lt; 75) = Φ(−1.25) ≈0.10565 . [M1] Use the normal model [M1] standardise 75 [A1] select the lower tail [A1] evaluate (b) The lower-tail probability 0.2266 has z ≈−0.7501, [B1] [A1] giving 85 + 8z ≈79.0 minutes . [M1] [A1] (c) The denominator uses (95 −85)/8 = 1.25. The intersection of X &lt; 75 and X &lt; 95 is X &lt; 75.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q7-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Since 75 &lt; 95, the conditional probability is P(X &lt; 75) P(X &lt; 95) = 0.1056498 . . . 0.8943502 . . . ≈0.1181 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 11 marks.</p>"
