  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-g/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"18N α 30° A box of weight 20 N is held by a rope, in limiting equilibrium on a fixed rough\" style=\"--madas-width:569.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"inclined plane. The rope is modelled as a light inextensible string and the box is modelled as a particle. The rope lies in a vertical plane containing a line of greatest slope of the incline plane 3 and is inclined to the plane at an angle α , where tan α = . 4 The plane is at an angle of 30° to the horizontal, as shown in the figure above. When the tension in the rope is 18 N the box is at the point of slipping up the plane. ( ) Calculate the value of the coefficient of friction between the box and the plane. 9\" style=\"--madas-width:597.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram: Since tan α = 3/4, the sine and cosine of α are 3/5 and 4/5. [B1] [A1] About-to-slip motion is up the slope, so limiting friction acts down the slope: [A1] Resolve perpendicular to the plane to find the normal reaction: R = 20 cos 30◦−18(3/5) √ [M1] [A1] = 10 3 −10.8.\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-g/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The perpendicular balance is R + 18 sin α = 20 cos 30◦. Resolve along the plane: F = 18(4/5) −20 sin 30◦ [M1] [A1] = 4.4. Here 18(4/5) = 14.4 and 20 sin 30◦= 10. Since F = µR, √ µ = 4.4/(10 3 −10.8) ≈0.675 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 9 marks.</p>"
